I kept both of my dundees.

1179
00:52:37.850 --> 00:52:41.650
I can promise you if I had been given a dundee that night, I would have it.

1180
00:52:41.910 --> 00:52:42.210
Mm-hmm.

1181
00:52:42.330 --> 00:52:43.690
We kept all of our dundees.

1182
00:52:43.830 --> 00:52:44.210
Of course.

1183
00:52:44.210 --> 00:52:45.710
We got to take them home with us.

1184
00:52:45.830 --> 00:52:49.850
On the way back to Dunder Mifflin, I guess D'Angelo really had to pee.

1185
00:52:50.090 --> 00:52:51.130
And he wanted to use the bathroom.

1186
00:52:51.210 --> 00:52:52.210
But Michael was like, no, it's close.

1187
00:52:52.350 --> 00:52:52.890
Just get in the car.

1188
00:52:53.050 --> 00:52:55.810
They're not going to get seats together in the conference room if they don't leave now.

1189
00:52:55.990 --> 00:52:56.170
Yeah.

1190
00:52:56.370 --> 00:52:57.830
And Dwight just starts to go off.

1191
00:52:57.990 --> 00:52:59.130
He goes off on D'Angelo.

1192
00:52:59.250 --> 00:53:03.830
He goes off on the dundees, what people wore, that the awards were stupid.

1193
00:53:03.970 --> 00:53:05.730
And Michael is ticked off.

1194
00:53:06.010 --> 00:53:06.190
Yeah.

1195
00:53:06.290 --> 00:53:07.630
They get in a pretty big argument.

1196
00:53:08.070 --> 00:53:10.430
And then Dwight gets out of the car and runs away.

1197
00:53:10.670 --> 00:53:14.810
Well, when everyone is walking in, you can see that Ryan has a dundee in his hand.

1198
00:53:14.990 --> 00:53:17.470
Now, I do remember he really did win a dundee.

1199
00:53:17.570 --> 00:53:18.990
We just got cut.

1200
00:53:18.990 --> 00:53:19.570
Yeah.

1201
00:53:19.810 --> 00:53:24.730
In the shooting draft, it says that Ryan wins the most classically handsome dundee.

1202
00:53:25.010 --> 00:53:25.230
Yes.

1203
00:53:25.470 --> 00:53:26.730
And he's very pleased with that.

1204
00:53:27.010 --> 00:53:30.510
Once we get in the conference room, Daryl has set up a keyboard in the corner.

1205
00:53:31.110 --> 00:53:33.790
And two awards are given in the conference room.

1206
00:53:34.030 --> 00:53:35.270
One was in the shooting draft.

1207
00:53:35.270 --> 00:53:36.350
We also filmed it.

1208
00:53:36.470 --> 00:53:37.410
It's in deleted scenes.

1209
00:53:37.790 --> 00:53:40.030
Daryl would have won the Moving On Up Award.

1210
00:53:40.030 --> 00:53:49.630
And then Michael is going to present Andy with the Doobie Doobie Pothead Stoner of the Year Award because he tried pot in college.

1211
00:53:49.810 --> 00:53:53.150
And oh, boy, this kicks off a moment.

1212
00:53:53.150 --> 00:53:54.830
What does it ever?

1213
00:53:55.110 --> 00:53:57.690
Andy accepts and he tells Michael, thank you.

1214
00:53:57.990 --> 00:54:00.750
And then he says, no, thank you for everything.

1215
00:54:01.070 --> 00:54:02.790
Did you hear Ed's voice crack?

1216
00:54:03.090 --> 00:54:03.870
I did.

1217
00:54:03.870 --> 00:54:06.790
Yeah, that's just real emotion.

1218
00:54:07.230 --> 00:54:07.530
Yeah.

1219
00:54:07.650 --> 00:54:12.670
If you go to 18 minutes, 53 seconds, he's emotional because he knows what's coming.

1220
00:54:13.810 --> 00:54:20.290
Music is going to start playing and everyone in the conference room is going to sing a tribute song to Michael.

1221
00:54:20.570 --> 00:54:26.290
We are going to sing a version of Seasons of Love from the musical Rent.

1222
00:54:26.690 --> 00:54:32.510
So, Jenna, right as the music starts, there would have been a cutaway Jim and Pam double talking head.

1223
00:54:32.970 --> 00:54:34.670
And I wanted to share it with you.

1224
00:54:35.450 --> 00:54:38.770
Jim says, we practiced every day after work in the warehouse.

1225
00:54:39.090 --> 00:54:42.150
And Pam says, we just thought it would be a nice thing to do.

1226
00:54:42.670 --> 00:54:45.270
And then it would cut back and everyone would start to sing.

1227
00:54:45.910 --> 00:54:50.450
Well, we practiced a lot as a cast for this moment.

1228
00:54:51.450 --> 00:54:53.610
And Angela, you thought we should hear this.

1229
00:54:53.790 --> 00:54:54.450
I do.

1230
00:54:54.930 --> 00:54:58.770
I mean, my memory was just it was so special to us.

1231
00:54:59.330 --> 00:55:05.110
You know, Phyllis and I had to sing together, Email Fords You Made Us Read.

1232
00:55:05.290 --> 00:55:05.890
I remember.

1233
00:55:06.090 --> 00:55:09.910
And we would meet in my trailer and practice, Email Fords You Made Us Read.

1234
00:55:09.950 --> 00:55:10.630
It's a lot.

1235
00:55:10.630 --> 00:55:14.590
We all got like a digital file with the music.

1236
00:55:14.890 --> 00:55:15.910
And we would do that.

1237
00:55:16.070 --> 00:55:20.290
We would just sing our little phrase and practice and practice and practice.

1238
00:55:20.630 --> 00:55:24.050
And because Phyllis and I had to do ours together, we would meet and practice.

1239
00:55:24.410 --> 00:55:26.130
Well, we got a fan mail flurry.

1240
00:55:26.410 --> 00:55:31.470
People wanted to know, is it true that the Seasons of Love parody, The Office Sings for Michael,

1241
00:55:31.590 --> 00:55:35.070
in this episode was actually a surprise for Steve Carell?

1242
00:55:36.510 --> 00:55:38.650
So, yes, it was.

1243
00:55:38.810 --> 00:55:39.450
Yes and no.

1244
00:55:39.650 --> 00:55:42.790
This story has gotten embellished.

1245
00:55:42.930 --> 00:55:47.310
So, the truth is, Steve knew this song existed.

1246
00:55:47.590 --> 00:55:49.230
It was in the shooting draft.

1247
00:55:49.330 --> 00:55:49.450
Yeah.

1248
00:55:49.530 --> 00:55:51.030
It was part of the table read.

1249
00:55:51.150 --> 00:55:51.310
Yeah.

1250
00:55:51.310 --> 00:55:53.690
But we practiced it privately.

1251
00:55:53.960 --> 00:55:56.210
He was never part of any rehearsals.

1252
00:55:56.390 --> 00:56:02.670
So, the first time he heard us sing together was in that room on the first take.

1253
00:56:03.050 --> 00:56:06.370
We even did our on-camera rehearsals without him.

1254
00:56:06.810 --> 00:56:06.970
Yeah.

1255
00:56:07.170 --> 00:56:11.490
So, what you see in Steve's face, you know, his emotion.

1256
00:56:12.070 --> 00:56:17.590
I mean, yes, he's a great actor, but also Steve, our friend, was watching all of our hard work

1257
00:56:17.590 --> 00:56:20.710
and just us showing him how much we loved him and we're going to miss him.

1258
00:56:21.410 --> 00:56:26.690
When I look at Steve's face in that scene, I see a person who's really in the moment,

1259
00:56:26.690 --> 00:56:31.310
who is taking in everything he's about to leave behind.

1260
00:56:31.650 --> 00:56:31.890
Yeah.

1261
00:56:32.650 --> 00:56:35.250
And I think he was feeling that in the moment.

1262
00:56:35.430 --> 00:56:38.690
I've actually talked to him about it, and he said it was incredibly moving.

1263
00:56:39.050 --> 00:56:39.250
Yeah.

1264
00:56:39.250 --> 00:56:40.890
And we all tear up.

1265
00:56:41.290 --> 00:56:44.130
In fact, Phyllis and I held hands for part of it.

1266
00:56:44.290 --> 00:56:45.950
I just think we need to hear it.

1267
00:56:51.940 --> 00:56:52.780
Dabby.

1268
00:56:55.460 --> 00:56:59.220
9,986,000 minutes.

1269
00:56:59.700 --> 00:57:03.780
We actually sat down and did the math.

1270
00:57:04.860 --> 00:57:08.740
9,986,000 minutes.

1271
00:57:09.480 --> 00:57:13.180
That's how many minutes that you've worked here.

1272
00:57:13.480 --> 00:57:14.620
In costumes.

1273
00:57:14.620 --> 00:57:15.660
And impressions.

1274
00:57:16.060 --> 00:57:17.020
In meetings.

1275
00:57:17.260 --> 00:57:18.840
In cups of coffee.

1276
00:57:19.160 --> 00:57:20.040
For birthdays.

1277
00:57:20.340 --> 00:57:21.540
More meetings and...

1278
00:57:21.540 --> 00:57:23.560
Email boards you've made us read.

1279
00:57:23.960 --> 00:57:27.780
9,986,000 minutes.

1280
00:57:28.380 --> 00:57:32.140
That's like watching Die Hard 80,000 times.

1281
00:57:32.620 --> 00:57:34.820
You hit me with your car.

1282
00:57:35.160 --> 00:57:37.060
You help me get off drugs.

1283
00:57:37.060 --> 00:57:39.440
I watch you when you sleep.

1284
00:57:39.940 --> 00:57:40.380
I watch you when you sleep.

1285
00:57:40.380 --> 00:57:41.880
I forgive you for kissing me.

1286
00:57:42.060 --> 00:57:44.080
Remember to call.

1287
00:57:48.200 --> 00:57:48.660
Call.

1288
00:57:58.000 --> 00:57:58.500
Measure.

1289
00:57:59.320 --> 00:58:00.740
Measure your love.

1290
00:58:06.090 --> 00:58:07.050
Remember to call.

1291
00:58:11.630 --> 00:58:12.010
To call.

1292
00:58:12.010 --> 00:58:20.820
I love it every time.

1293
00:58:20.820 --> 00:58:22.060
I just love it.

1294
00:58:22.420 --> 00:58:28.420
I want you guys to know in the shooting draft, right after D'Angelo hits that super high note,

1295
00:58:29.100 --> 00:58:31.880
there was a talking head written for him where he would have said,

1296
00:58:32.320 --> 00:58:35.920
I'm not a good performer, but I can sing like a f***ing angel.

1297
00:58:39.120 --> 00:58:42.660
Well, we got a lot of fan mail flurries about this song, Angela.

1298
00:58:42.920 --> 00:58:47.680
And one of the biggest was something I did not notice until I read our mail.

1299
00:58:47.880 --> 00:58:49.040
I don't know how I missed it.

1300
00:58:49.080 --> 00:58:50.860
I think I was just overcome with emotion.

1301
00:58:51.580 --> 00:58:57.620
But fans pointed out that Rainn Wilson, as Dwight, was not in the scene.

1302
00:58:57.840 --> 00:58:59.840
It's crazy to think about.

1303
00:59:00.460 --> 00:59:00.840
Yeah.

1304
00:59:01.040 --> 00:59:03.580
And they said, we get why he wasn't in the scene.

1305
00:59:03.740 --> 00:59:05.540
It's because in the scene prior, he gets mad.

1306
00:59:05.540 --> 00:59:06.600
He gets out of the car.

1307
00:59:06.800 --> 00:59:12.440
But people said, considering how monumental a scene this was for both the show and the cast,

1308
00:59:12.560 --> 00:59:14.420
it really feels like he is missing.

1309
00:59:15.000 --> 00:59:20.380
A lot of people felt that it should have been Dwight standing next to Michael instead of D'Angelo.

1310
00:59:21.220 --> 00:59:24.760
And people were hoping maybe Mindy could make sense of this.

1311
00:59:24.900 --> 00:59:26.400
And here's what she had to say.

1312
00:59:27.120 --> 00:59:34.000
This is a question that you said a lot of people sent in, which was why wasn't Rainn a part of the song?

1313
00:59:34.120 --> 00:59:38.380
We know why Dwight wasn't in the scene because in the scene prior, he stormed out of the car.

1314
00:59:38.760 --> 00:59:40.260
So it makes sense he wasn't there.

1315
00:59:40.360 --> 00:59:44.740
But considering how monumental a scene this was for both the show and the cast, it really feels like he's missing.

1316
00:59:45.340 --> 00:59:48.780
And so I have to say, I think this is a taste thing.

1317
00:59:48.780 --> 00:59:49.420
Um,

1318
00:59:50.340 --> 01:00:01.700
I think that if it didn't make sense emotionally in the episode for him to be there and I think that orchestrating it so that Dwight would be there when it didn't make sense for his character would have,

1319
01:00:01.820 --> 01:00:03.020
I think, been a bridge too far.

1320
01:00:03.020 --> 01:00:12.700
But I did feel like emotionally, it's like what the cast, the actors, and also the characters sort of wanted to express.

1321
01:00:13.000 --> 01:00:16.540
And we knew that like Steve is so good when Michael's emotional.

1322
01:00:16.680 --> 01:00:17.820
He's like and gets touched.

1323
01:00:18.040 --> 01:00:20.340
So and it just felt like it was nearing the end.

1324
01:00:20.460 --> 01:00:21.200
So it needed to happen.

1325
01:00:21.340 --> 01:00:22.660
But that's my answer to that.

1326
01:00:22.660 --> 01:00:28.320
Well, we were really curious what it must have been like to direct such a huge moment.

1327
01:00:28.400 --> 01:00:30.120
And we asked Mindy about it.

1328
01:00:30.260 --> 01:00:31.200
Here's what she had to say.

1329
01:00:31.700 --> 01:00:37.960
I have to say it is so hard to direct an emotional goodbye like this.

1330
01:00:38.140 --> 01:00:45.700
So much harder than directing a fight or even people kissing or romance and obviously harder, anything harder than comedy.

1331
01:00:45.700 --> 01:00:53.540
Because in comedy, you kind of know when you have a scene, but in something emotional, when everyone's coming together to sing, it's very hard to give notes.

1332
01:00:53.760 --> 01:00:59.740
Because if it, if everyone is like feeling it so emotionally, and then you have a lot of notes, people kind of don't want to hear it.

1333
01:00:59.820 --> 01:01:00.780
They're like, don't be a drag.

1334
01:01:00.940 --> 01:01:02.200
We're all like in our feelings.

1335
01:01:03.360 --> 01:01:08.200
And so that was, I think, one of the unique challenges of this episode.

1336
01:01:08.360 --> 01:01:09.080
I hear that.

1337
01:01:09.360 --> 01:01:09.720
Yeah.

1338
01:01:09.720 --> 01:01:16.940
I also know as a cast, we were so gutted and we were in our feelings.

1339
01:01:17.240 --> 01:01:17.560
We were.

1340
01:01:18.100 --> 01:01:18.440
Yeah.

1341
01:01:18.640 --> 01:01:22.020
We got one final fan mail flurry about this scene.

1342
01:01:22.240 --> 01:01:24.380
People wanted to know who wrote the song.

1343
01:01:24.780 --> 01:01:32.040
Well, Mindy wrote the lyrics and Randy said that Eve Nelson, our go-to composer, created that instrumental track that we sang along to.

1344
01:01:32.340 --> 01:01:36.460
And we paid a royalty fee of $25,000 for the rights to the music.

1345
01:01:36.460 --> 01:01:43.160
And people also wanted to know, is that an accurate number of minutes that Michael would have worked in the office?

1346
01:01:43.160 --> 01:01:46.500
Or was it the number of minutes that Steve worked on the show?

1347
01:01:46.680 --> 01:01:48.420
Well, Ange, I got out my calculator.

1348
01:01:48.720 --> 01:01:49.720
You did the math.

1349
01:01:49.840 --> 01:01:50.260
I did.

1350
01:01:50.580 --> 01:01:54.580
So what I did was I counted all the episodes that Steve has been in.

1351
01:01:54.720 --> 01:02:01.220
And I assumed that we, on average, we work about 60 hours a week per episode.

1352
01:02:01.220 --> 01:02:04.960
So I added all that up and did the minutes.

1353
01:02:05.160 --> 01:02:10.780
And I can tell you, it's not the number of minutes that Steve worked on the show.

1354
01:02:10.940 --> 01:02:12.200
It wasn't enough minutes.

1355
01:02:12.460 --> 01:02:17.520
So I'm going with the answer is it's the number of minutes Michael has worked at Dunder Mifflin.

1356
01:02:17.680 --> 01:02:23.300
Because also, Michael has worked at Dunder Mifflin more than seven years, which is how long Steve worked on the show.

1357
01:02:24.580 --> 01:02:26.760
So I hope that clears things up for everyone.

1358
01:02:26.760 --> 01:02:28.540
It was about 10 minutes of math.

1359
01:02:28.720 --> 01:02:32.720
I was going to say, how long did it take you to come to your conclusion?

1360
01:02:33.440 --> 01:02:34.260
About 10 minutes.

1361
01:02:34.280 --> 01:02:34.580
About 10 minutes.

1362
01:02:34.620 --> 01:02:37.920
I mean, because I was trying to figure out a lot of things.

1363
01:02:38.080 --> 01:02:40.140
I had to count episodes.

1364
01:02:40.440 --> 01:02:41.580
I would say that's impressive.

1365
01:02:41.720 --> 01:02:43.660
I think it would have taken me longer than 10 minutes.

1366
01:02:43.920 --> 01:02:46.360
Maybe I'll get a Dundee for best calculator work.

1367
01:02:46.540 --> 01:02:46.920
Yes.

1368
01:02:47.780 --> 01:02:49.200
Next year, you'll have to see.

1369
01:02:49.860 --> 01:02:51.520
I'm on the edge of my seat.

1370
01:02:52.500 --> 01:02:54.520
Well, the episode is going to end with a tag.

1371
01:02:54.760 --> 01:03:01.500
It's a flashback to earlier in the evening because Toby is going to win the Extreme Repulsiveness Award.

1372
01:03:02.200 --> 01:03:03.580
D'Angelo is reading the cue card.

1373
01:03:03.700 --> 01:03:04.520
He's like, wait, what am I?

1374
01:03:04.640 --> 01:03:06.160
He's like, what does this kind of mean?

1375
01:03:07.260 --> 01:03:08.820
Toby doesn't want to go accept it.

1376
01:03:08.900 --> 01:03:10.880
But Oscar's like, it's his last Dundees, man.

1377
01:03:11.060 --> 01:03:11.860
You got to play along.

1378
01:03:12.060 --> 01:03:12.200
Yeah.

1379
01:03:12.300 --> 01:03:18.220
And he's going to use his acceptance speech to come clean about the Scranton Strangler case for which he was a juror.

1380
01:03:18.220 --> 01:03:22.720
And they found this person guilty and he's been given the death penalty, we find out.

1381
01:03:23.200 --> 01:03:25.420
Toby's now not so sure that guy really did it.

1382
01:03:25.620 --> 01:03:26.580
And that's how it ends.

1383
01:03:26.660 --> 01:03:26.840
Yeah.

1384
01:03:26.960 --> 01:03:29.060
It almost ends like mid-sentence.

1385
01:03:29.140 --> 01:03:29.300
Yeah.

1386
01:03:29.520 --> 01:03:31.280
Like when I was watching it, I was like, wait, wait, that's it?

1387
01:03:31.620 --> 01:03:33.900
Well, that was Michael's last Dundees.

1388
01:03:34.060 --> 01:03:37.940
I've got a few extra tidbits here for the end of the episode.

1389
01:03:37.940 --> 01:03:41.600
I didn't know where to put this information, so I'll tell it to you now.

1390
01:03:42.260 --> 01:03:46.200
This episode was originally titled Goodbye, Michael, Part 1.

1391
01:03:46.440 --> 01:03:56.420
But it was renamed and given a new release date when NBC announced that Goodbye, Michael, Steve's actual final episode, could be a supersized episode.

1392
01:03:56.800 --> 01:03:59.280
So then this became Michael's last Dundees.

1393
01:03:59.280 --> 01:04:07.500
But the original goodbye to Steve Carell on our show was going to be Dundees that flowed into Goodbye, Michael.

1394
01:04:07.840 --> 01:04:07.940
Yeah.

1395
01:04:08.680 --> 01:04:11.020
My gosh, we're literally speaking in unison.

1396
01:04:12.160 --> 01:04:17.420
I also thought you might be wondering what Miles McNutt thought about this episode.

1397
01:04:17.820 --> 01:04:27.140
I have to tell you, from the very beginning of the episode, when you did Fast Facts, I thought for sure one of your Fast Facts was going to be what Miles McNutt thought of it.

1398
01:04:27.140 --> 01:04:28.880
But I have been waiting this whole episode.

1399
01:04:28.880 --> 01:04:29.820
I can't wait to hear.

1400
01:04:30.080 --> 01:04:31.500
It was going to be.

1401
01:04:31.680 --> 01:04:32.200
It was.

1402
01:04:32.340 --> 01:04:37.940
But then yesterday, you asked me if you could have Fast Facts number three, so I had to move this information to the end of the episode.

1403
01:04:38.380 --> 01:04:40.500
But I was not going to leave you hanging.

1404
01:04:40.720 --> 01:04:41.220
Trust me.

1405
01:04:42.440 --> 01:04:44.260
Miles McNutt gave it a B minus.

1406
01:04:45.460 --> 01:04:46.200
B minus.

1407
01:04:46.360 --> 01:04:49.580
He said he really liked the cold open and the closing song.

1408
01:04:51.880 --> 01:04:56.680
But a lot of his review focused on comparing the two Dundee episodes.

1409
01:04:56.680 --> 01:04:59.340
And he felt that the first one was superior.

1410
01:04:59.820 --> 01:05:04.540
And it was very hard to live in its shadow, in Miles's estimation.

1411
01:05:04.960 --> 01:05:09.200
Miles, so much more is happening in this episode than in the first Dundees.

1412
01:05:10.320 --> 01:05:12.840
Your lead character is leaving the show.

1413
01:05:13.000 --> 01:05:14.500
You have a lot of ground to cover.

1414
01:05:15.180 --> 01:05:16.800
Miles, I think you're being too harsh.

1415
01:05:17.040 --> 01:05:19.500
I will end this with a letter from Autumn B.

1416
01:05:19.640 --> 01:05:21.200
in Wisconsin, who said,

1417
01:05:21.600 --> 01:05:23.420
Incredible women of office, ladies.

1418
01:05:24.120 --> 01:05:24.960
Thank you.

1419
01:05:24.960 --> 01:05:25.600
Thank you, Autumn.

1420
01:05:25.920 --> 01:05:29.220
After watching Michael's last Dundees, I watched the first one.

1421
01:05:30.080 --> 01:05:32.020
Please, please do this.

1422
01:05:32.600 --> 01:05:37.400
Watching these two episodes back to back illuminates the evolution of Michael Scott.

1423
01:05:37.600 --> 01:05:45.420
A man yearning for belonging and acceptance becomes a man who has found his place, his confidence, his people, and his purpose.

1424
01:05:45.420 --> 01:05:52.920
The contrast between the first and the last Dundees brings hope and comfort to all of us who believe that with time and conviction,

1425
01:05:52.920 --> 01:05:56.980
we will become better versions of ourselves and live our best lives.

1426
01:05:56.980 --> 01:06:03.880
Of all people, it was Michael Scott who would have thought, take that, Miles McNutt.

1427
01:06:04.000 --> 01:06:05.300
That's what I'm saying.

1428
01:06:05.540 --> 01:06:06.260
Go on them.

1429
01:06:06.260 --> 01:06:10.860
I think you cannot compare one Dundees to another.

1430
01:06:11.220 --> 01:06:13.160
You have to put them together.

1431
01:06:13.440 --> 01:06:14.480
Marry them.

1432
01:06:14.680 --> 01:06:14.960
Mm-hmm.

1433
01:06:15.180 --> 01:06:16.440
Watch them together.

1434
01:06:16.700 --> 01:06:17.120
Mm-hmm.

1435
01:06:17.620 --> 01:06:20.280
And there you have your A plus.

1436
01:06:22.050 --> 01:06:22.950
Pen drop.

1437
01:06:23.130 --> 01:06:24.970
I did a visual bit on our podcaSt.

1438
01:06:25.330 --> 01:06:25.510
You sure did.

1439
01:06:25.770 --> 01:06:26.850
You sure did.

1440
01:06:26.850 --> 01:06:29.170
It's your special talent.

1441
01:06:30.030 --> 01:06:32.550
You guys, that was Michael's last Dundees.

1442
01:06:32.730 --> 01:06:33.370
Big thank you.

1443
01:06:33.830 --> 01:06:34.310
Oh!

1444
01:06:36.150 --> 01:06:40.230
Big thank you to Mindy Kaling for sending in audio clips.

1445
01:06:40.490 --> 01:06:42.990
Thank you, Randy Cordray, for all your tidbits.

1446
01:06:43.430 --> 01:06:48.550
Thank you to Sam and Cassie and Angela, our very own Michael Scott.

1447
01:06:49.070 --> 01:06:50.230
Have a great week.

1448
01:06:50.390 --> 01:06:53.670
We're taking next week off, but we'll be back with Goodbye, Michael.

1449
01:06:54.030 --> 01:06:54.830
Oh, my goodness.

1450
01:06:55.190 --> 01:06:56.190
Oh, no, I'm not ready.

1451
01:07:05.300 --> 01:07:06.960
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.

1452
01:07:07.260 --> 01:07:11.160
Office Ladies is produced by Earwolf, Jenna Fisher, and Angela Kinsey.

1453
01:07:11.440 --> 01:07:14.100
Our show is executive produced by Cody Fisher.

1454
01:07:14.400 --> 01:07:16.480
Our producer is Cassie Jerkins.

1455
01:07:16.660 --> 01:07:18.480
Our sound engineer is Sam Kiefer.

1456
01:07:18.720 --> 01:07:21.000
And our associate producer is Ainsley Bubba Coe.

1457
01:07:21.220 --> 01:07:24.080
Our theme song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.

